G_DEFINE_ABSTRACT_TYPE leaves a parent_class behind that nothing reads
when the type never chains up, and this clang has only lately started
warning about it. pango turns that warning into an error after CFLAGS
have had their say, so it cannot be waved off from make.conf.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -147,7 +147,6 @@
     '-Werror=int-to-pointer-cast',
     '-Werror=empty-body',
     '-Werror=write-strings',
-    '-Werror=unused-but-set-variable',
     '-Wundef', # FIXME: https://bugzilla.gnome.org/show_bug.cgi?id=792481
   ]
 
